-- title:
--   A fully iterated form identity gives a terminal CFZ certificate
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ne0$, fix $\nu:\mathbb Z/N\mathbb Z\to\mathbb R$ and a face $j$, and let $S$ be a majorized cut system over finite types with arity $n$. Suppose a Boolean linear-forms exponent pattern selects no factor on $j$, and for every finite-type presentation of the terminal stage parameter the fully iterated form equals the mean of the centered face product on $j$ times that selected linear-forms product. Then $S$ has a terminal CFZ certificate.
